 *   **Looser Tree:** Omitting min/max pairs at leaf nodes generates a looser tree, which theoretically hurts performance [S2, S3]. However, in practice, this forces the computation of forward voxel extrema during neighbor-finding, which is already required for cell reconstruction [S2, S3].
 *   **Storage Overhead:** Storing min/max pairs for every scalar voxel would demand over three times the storage of the raw octree data [S2, S3]. The optimization of starting at $d_{max}-1$ keeps overhead to ~22% [S2, S3].
-*   **Forward Neighbor Definition:** The definition of "forward neighbors" is critical and relies on the hashing scheme from the parent article [S2, S3]. Incorrect neighbor lookup leads to incorrect bounding volumes.
