 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Construction is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of nodes, as each node is processed once during bottom-up consolidation [S1, S3]. Ray traversal is accelerated by the min/max checks, reducing the number of cells intersected.
+*   **Time Complexity:** Construction is performed simultaneously with bottom-up consolidation, processing each node once [S1, S3]. Ray traversal is accelerated by the min/max checks, allowing early rejection of children without traversal and sparing cache misses [S3].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Adds approximately 22% overhead to the raw scalar octree-compressed data [S2, S3].
 *   **Strengths:** Accurately bounds cell-based primitives, enabling efficient culling during ray traversal. The storage overhead is acceptable given the acceleration gains [S2, S3].
